"Licensor" means SCM Jakub Berechowski (NIP PL8133936176), a business
registered in the Republic of Poland.

"Software" means the scm_ifirma PrestaShop module and all files distributed
with it.

"You" / "Your" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under
this License.

"Consumer" means a natural person using the Software for purposes not directly
related to their business or professional activity (within the meaning of
art. 22(1) of the Polish Civil Code).

"Small or Medium-Sized Business (SMB)" means a natural person conducting
business activity or a legal entity that, at the time of installation and
during continued use, satisfies ALL of the following:
  (a) fewer than 250 employees (full-time equivalents), AND
  (b) annual gross revenue below EUR 50,000,000 (fifty million euros) or the
      equivalent in any other currency, AND
  (c) is not majority-owned or controlled by an entity that does not itself
      qualify as an SMB under (a) and (b).

"Enterprise" means any entity that does NOT qualify as an SMB.

"Commercial Use" means use in a revenue-generating context, including but not
limited to: operating an online store, providing services to paying customers,
or internal use within a for-profit organisation. Commercial Use does not
include the activities listed under "Non-Commercial Use" below.

"Non-Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is not Commercial Use,
including but not limited to:
  (a) personal, private, or hobby use by a natural person;
  (b) use for education, teaching, academic study, or scientific research;
  (c) use by non-profit organisations, charities, foundations, associations,
      public institutions, and open-source projects within their activities
      that do not generate revenue;
  (d) evaluation, testing, development, debugging, and demonstration of the
      Software on non-production installations (such as local, development,
      or staging environments), regardless of who performs them.
A use ceases to be Non-Commercial Use the moment the Software is put into
productive use in a revenue-generating context (for example, a live store
issuing real invoices or receipts).

"Modified Version" means any copy of the Software in which any file — source
code, templates, scripts, styles, SQL, translations, or otherwise — has been
altered by You or on Your behalf, including any derivative work based on the
Software.

